// THREE IDENTITIES ENROLLED 2026-08-23, and they are the first rows here that were AUTHORED red
// rather than discovered red. They are compiler control fixtures: each hands the v1 compile path a
// program the host refuses at evaluation and asserts that the refusal happens at COMPILE. All three
// return false today, measured by execution at head 907f19c2cc.
//
// WHY THEY WERE AUTHORED. Required-floor run 32633501354 reported known_red_runtime_errored=164 --
// programs the compiler accepted and the interpreter could not evaluate -- and that counter is the
// class's only observer. It falls to zero as the 164 witnesses are repaired, taking the evidence
// with it, so the class needed evidence that does not live in the specimens. Eleven of the 164 are
// this family: a host primitive's argument list is not checked at compile in any direction.
//
// WHY THEY BELONG IN A ROSTER WHOSE HEADER SAYS A ROW BELONGS HERE ONLY WHILE SOMEONE IS FIXING IT.
// Nobody is fixing this one today, and the enrolment is still the honest home rather than a
// demotion: the roster's stale-quarantine arm is exactly what these rows need, because the day the
// argument contract is checked at compile they PASS and red the build naming themselves. That arm
// is the whole point of authoring them as reds instead of as assertions of today's behaviour, which
// would have been a change detector pointing the wrong way.
//
// THE THREE ROWS STAY ENROLLED HERE AS THE AUTHORED REDS THEY ARE. Their home currently declares
// ReadsLiveTree and is declined before execution, so floor_expected_red_is_live excludes them from
// the live roster until that decline is removed. Keeping identity and temporary liveness separate
// preserves the enrolment and gives the coupling below one mechanism rather than two accounts.
//
// The partition of the 164 and the measurements behind this family are
// docs/plans/receipts/floor-runtime-error-partition-2026-08-23/.
// ONE IDENTITY ENROLLED 2026-08-26 with a per-row reason, because a row without one is how a
// thrown claim gets filed as a semantic red. THE CLASS: a lexical binding holding a NON-CALLABLE
// value, called at its own spelling, still falls through to the module free function sharing that
// spelling and returns ITS answer -- a plausible wrong value with no diagnostic. It is the
// unrepaired half of the local-binding-shadow class whose callable half landed the same day; the
// witness's own annotation carries the two-tier disagreement that makes it legible (the compile
// sibling already refuses a labeled call through this exact binding, naming the callee a function
// value, while dispatch walks past it). THE ROW ASSERTS THE DESIRED LAW, so it reds now and greens
// on repair, and its single conjunct returns a Bool and never throws -- an OBSERVED semantic red,
// never no-verdict debt. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the census of non-callable lexical bindings whose
// spelling collides with a builtin or module free function; the gate is widened against a measured
// population, never speculatively.
